#
# The simulation gate battery: one gate per line, each naming a
# scripts/cli_<gate>_test.sh. This file is the LIST; scripts/run_gates.sh is
# the runner. They are separate because two different readers need the list:
# the runner, and scripts/check_orphan_gates.py, which proves that every
# cli_*_test.sh in the tree is actually reachable from here. A gate script
# that no list names is dead code that still looks like coverage.
#
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Adding a gate script WITHOUT
# adding it here is what check_orphan_gates.py fails on.
#
# Needs Vivado XSIM -- this battery is not runnable on a stock CI runner; see
# the "Continuous integration" section of CONTRIBUTING.md.

# --- overflow / robustness gates -------------------------------------------
natovf
jtcovf
irovf
bphws
